The exploratory IRT model will always fit better than a confirmatory one in terms of log-likelihood criteria (it is a highly over-parameterized model). Regarding your questions

1. If you translate this into a type of Q-matrix and pass that to mirt.model() then you could get this structure automatically.

2. Not that I can see. F2 might be a little under-defined empirically, but it could be fine if the correlations between the auxillary traits is reasonably high (that would help with stability).

Phil

