Hi Phil,

I'm trying to simulate the d parameters for a multidimensional GPCM model. I see the codes below in the manual to simulate the d parameters for a unidimensional graded model. Do you have any suggestions (e.g., mean, sd, relations between d1, d2, d3 ) to simulate the d parameters of a multidimensional GPCM (for example, 3 score categories (0,1,2))? Thanks a lot!

# for the graded model, ensure that there is enough space between the intercepts,
# otherwise closer categories will not be selected often (minimum distance of 0.3 here)
diffs <- t <https://rdrr.io/r/base/t.html>(apply <https://rdrr.io/r/base/apply.html>(matrix <https://rdrr.io/r/base/matrix.html>(runif <https://rdrr.io/r/stats/Uniform.html>(20*4, .3, 1), 20), 1, cumsum <https://rdrr.io/r/base/cumsum.html>))
diffs <- -(diffs - rowMeans <https://rdrr.io/r/base/colSums.html>(diffs))
d <- diffs + rnorm <https://rdrr.io/r/stats/Normal.html>(20)

